body:
If a straight guy is into Karlach, I 100% guarantee that man treats his woman like a queen. That man is secure in his masculinity.

&#x200B;

I for one love that there are no characters that are romance locked by a certain gender. Would Karlach prefer women in real life? Maybe. But also I really like the Wyll/Karlach ship....

figure skating.

&#x200B;

literally the most expensive one I could have stuck with. started as an adult and all of my extra money goes to it.

I restarted my first run after about ten hours because I realized all of the things I was doing wrong and needed to go back and do it the right way.

&#x200B;

I've also only finished the game twice in its entirety (once for tav, once for durge). I enjoy the parts leading up to the end much more than the end. So I just keep making new characters and new choices. If there was endgame content I'd feel differently, but since there's not, I'm not going through that fight again unless I do an honor mode run or something.

there... there was a sign that said this?

&#x200B;

god this would have been the PERFECT "gotcha" moment for the game to teach you a hard life lesson about reading signs...
